---
layout: layouts/dark.njk
title: Cabbage Coins | Auction Representation
permalink: /auction-representation/
description: Existing Cabbage Coins customers can have Tony bid for them at coin auctions on coins of $2,000 and up. 3% at online-only auctions; 5% (3% over $25,000) at auctions with in-person lot viewing. Nothing if you don't win.
---
<section class="cc26-pagehero">
    <div class="cc26-wrap cc26-pagehero__in">
        <div class="cc26-eyebrow">Auction representation</div>
        <h1>Let Tony bid for you.</h1>
        <p class="cc26-lede">Found a coin in an upcoming auction? Cabbage Coins can bid on your behalf, take delivery from the auction house, and ship the coin to you fully insured. You only pay a fee on coins you win.</p>
        <div class="cc26-hero__ctas">
            <button type="button" class="cc26-btn cc26-btn--gold cc26-btn--lg" data-modal-open="cc26-contact">Ask Tony to bid for you</button>
            <a class="cc26-textlink" href="/consignment/">Selling instead? See consignment</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="cc26-wrap cc26-section">
    <article class="cc26-service">
        <img class="cc26-service__img" src="/assets/img/services-auction.jpg" alt="Tony inspecting a coin with a loupe at a show table" loading="lazy" width="1400" height="1050" style="object-position: 40% 50%">
        <div class="cc26-service__body">
            <h2>How it works</h2>
            <ul class="cc26-checks">
                <li>For customers who have already done business with Cabbage Coins, on coins of $2,000 or more.</li>
                <li>Contact Tony with the auction, the lot numbers and your maximum bid for each lot.</li>
                <li>Tony places the bids in Cabbage Coins' name and never goes over your maximum.</li>
                <li>If you win, you pay the auction's invoice amount plus our fee. Cabbage Coins pays the auction house and takes delivery.</li>
                <li>Your coin ships to you insured, with a signature required.</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="cc26-tiers">
                <div class="cc26-tier">
                    <div class="cc26-tier__copy">
                        <h3>Online-only auctions</h3>
                        <p>Lots are viewed and bid on online only. A percentage of the price realized: the hammer price plus the auction's buyer's fee.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="cc26-tier__price">3%<span> of price realized</span><small>coins $2,000 and up</small></div>
                </div>
                <div class="cc26-tier">
                    <div class="cc26-tier__copy">
                        <h3>Auctions with in-person viewing</h3>
                        <p>Major sales where the lots can be viewed in person, so Tony can look at the coin for you before bidding.</p>
                        <p class="cc26-tier__note">3% on any coin whose price realized is over $25,000.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="cc26-tier__price">5%<span> of price realized</span><small>coins $2,000 and up</small></div>
                </div>
                <div class="cc26-tier">
                    <div class="cc26-tier__copy">
                        <h3>Coins you don't win</h3>
                        <p>No charge.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="cc26-tier__price">$0</div>
                </div>
                <div class="cc26-tier">
                    <div class="cc26-tier__copy">
                        <h3>Shipping to you</h3>
                        <p>Insured shipping with a signature required, billed at our actual cost.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="cc26-tier__price">At cost</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <p class="cc26-tier__note">The auction's buyer's fee is charged by the auction house, not by Cabbage Coins. Example: a coin that hammers at $10,000 with a 20% buyer's fee has a price realized of $12,000, so our fee is $360 at an online-only auction, or $600 at an auction with in-person viewing.</p>
        </div>
    </article>
</section>

<section class="cc26-wrap cc26-section cc26-section--last">
    <div class="cc26-cta">
        <div class="cc26-cta__copy">
            <div class="cc26-eyebrow">Have a lot in mind?</div>
            <h2>Tell Tony the auction, the lots and your maximum bids.</h2>
            <p>Please reach out a few days before the sale so there's time to talk it through.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cc26-cta__actions">
            <button type="button" class="cc26-btn cc26-btn--gold cc26-btn--lg" data-modal-open="cc26-contact">Contact Tony</button>
            <a class="cc26-textlink" href="tel:17177239505">(717) 723-9505</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

